    <main id="conteudo"><section class="page-hero condo-page-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span>Condominium charging management</p><h1>Shared EV charger management for condominiums</h1><p class="page-hero-copy">Bring residents, charger scheduling, manual consumption records and cost allocation into one private condominium hub.</p><a class="hero-play-cta" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=br.com.vevolt" rel="noopener"><span>Try VeVolt Condo free for 15 days</span><img src="/assets/google-play-badge-en.png" width="564" height="168" alt="Get it on Google Play"></a>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="feature-split"><div class="feature-copy"><p class="kicker">VeVolt Condo</p><h2>The administrator organizes. Residents join by invitation.</h2><p>The administrator subscribes to VeVolt Condo, creates the hub and invites residents. Invited residents participate without Premium, check schedules and record their usage.</p><div class="trial-offer"><p>New VeVolt Condo monthly customers get a separate 15-day trial. Then the local price shown by Google Play applies. Cancel anytime.</p><small>The annual plan remains available without a second free trial.</small></div><ul class="check-list"><li>Up to 50 participants</li><li>Up to 10 chargers</li><li>Invitations and schedule</li><li>Conflict-free time slots</li><li>Session and cost tracking</li><li>Manual consumption and allocation</li><li>Invited residents join without Premium</li></ul><a class="play-badge-link" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=br.com.vevolt" rel="noopener" aria-label="Get it on Google Play"><img src="/assets/google-play-badge-en.png" width="564" height="168" alt="Get it on Google Play"></a></div><picture class="app-phone">
    <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/app/en-condo-360.webp 360w, /assets/app/en-condo-720.webp 720w" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 86vw, 320px">
    <img src="/assets/app-en-condo.png" width="1080" height="1920" alt="VeVolt Condo" loading="eager" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
  </picture></div></div></section>
  <section class="section accent-band"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">VeVolt Condo</p><h2>A clear workflow for property managers and residents.</h2></div></div><div class="grid two"><article class="content-card"><h3>Property managers and administrators</h3><p>Centralize usage rules, invitations, private chargers, schedules and monthly review without scattered spreadsheets.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>Residents</h3><p>Join by invitation, view available times, schedule a shared charger and manually record each session.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">VeVolt Condo</p><h2>How shared charger management works.</h2></div><p>VeVolt Condo organizes the administrative workflow without interfering with the electrical installation.</p></div><div class="grid two"><article class="content-card"><h3>1. Create the hub</h3><p>Register the condominium and invite participants.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>2. Add chargers</h3><p>Organize up to 10 private chargers.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>3. Manage schedules</h3><p>Residents book conflict-free time slots.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>4. Review the period</h3><p>Use manually entered sessions, consumption and cost records to support allocation.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section accent-band"><div class="wrap"><div class="grid two"><article class="content-card"><h2>Scheduling and shared charger rules.</h2><p>Keep reservations and rules visible without booking public charging stations or changing charger power.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h2>Manual consumption and cost allocation.</h2><p>Residents manually enter session consumption and cost. VeVolt organizes the records for review; it does not meter or bill energy automatically.</p></article></div><div class="notice condo-limits"><strong>What VeVolt Condo does — and does not do.</strong><p>VeVolt Condo organizes up to 50 participants and 10 chargers. It does not physically control chargers, meter energy automatically, bill energy, run OCPP or perform load balancing. Electrical design, installation, metering and safety remain external responsibilities.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Blog VeVolt</p><h2>Condominium charging guides</h2></div><p>Explore rules, scheduling, cost allocation and manual tracking.</p></div><div class="grid two"><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>Electric-car charging in a condominium: what to organize</h3><p>Understand electrical assessment, approval, safety, scheduling, consumption records and cost allocation for shared EV charging.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/electric-car-charger-in-condominium">Read article →</a></div></article><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>Condominium EV charging management: organizing chargers and residents</h3><p>A practical workflow for property managers to organize residents, shared chargers, schedules, manual session records and cost allocation.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/condominium-ev-charging-management">Read article →</a></div></article><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>How to allocate EV charging costs in a condominium</h3><p>Define data sources, rates, review steps and manual records for fair and transparent shared EV charging cost allocation.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/allocate-ev-charging-costs-condominium">Read article →</a></div></article><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>Shared EV charger in a condominium: rules, booking and usage</h3><p>Create practical booking, delay, session and responsibility rules for residents sharing an EV charger.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/shared-ev-charger-condominium-rules">Read article →</a></div></article><article class="article-card"><div class="article-card-body"><h3>App to book an EV charger in a condominium</h3><p>Organize residents, conflict-free charging times, sessions and manual consumption records in one private condominium hub.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/blog/app-to-book-condominium-ev-charger">Read article →</a></div></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section accent-band"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">FAQ</p><h2>Shared condominium charging questions.</h2></div></div><div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item"><summary>How many residents and chargers can I organize?</summary><p>One VeVolt Condo hub supports up to 50 participants and 10 private chargers.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Does an invited resident need Premium?</summary><p>No. Premium and Condo are separate subscriptions, and invited residents join without Premium.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Who can use the free trial?</summary><p>The 15-day trial applies to eligible new customers of the monthly Condo plan. The annual plan has no second trial.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Does VeVolt meter or bill energy automatically?</summary><p>No. Consumption and costs are entered manually and reviewed by the condominium.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Does VeVolt control chargers through OCPP?</summary><p>No. It does not run OCPP, switch hardware or perform load balancing.</p></details></div></div></section>
